sitories.\n- [APPROVE] TC-383 -> the obligation: drive the record rule over real commits, lane walks, staged trees and squash landings. The close and an unchanged carriage pass. Hand-written, unequal, changed or removed records, a rewritten request under a carried record, an invalid parent-tree adoption, a requesting move without a record, and an unreadable parent each refuse. A merge is judged only on its novel changes, and the real close admits only its exact inbound relinks outside `docs/work` -> what its chain shows: it verifies SR-148, LLR-345, IF-303 and IF-304 through 21 named cases, which match the Done-when's commit-check arms one for one -> why it is ready: Expected names the admitted set and its closure, and every LLR-345 arm has a case.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=4\n\n## Dispositions\n\n```toml\ntitle = \"WI-969 spine rework: LLR-153's title-lineage refusal, TC-147 and TC-156's replay citation; re-sit the three amendments\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = [\"SR-148\", \"SR-174\"]\nneeds = [\"WI-969\"]\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\nbuildtier = \"quick\"\n```\n\nThis is spine text only; no code change is called for.\n1. **LLR-153:** state the mismatch outcome in the new sentence: a standing row found by exact title whose lineage differs from the draft's refuses the mint before any write, while one on the draft's own lineage stands. This is WI-902's Trust ruling.\n2. **TC-147 and TC-156:** cite the requirement that actually states full-successor replay (LLR-153's replay clause, and LLR-335's single lineage operation) rather than \"SR-148\".\n3. **TC-156:** trim its Method's mint arms (no id, title and lineage, replay) to the handback arms its own adoption cases hold, or cite LLR-153 for them. TC-147 already verifies those arms.\n\nThen re-sit LLR-153, TC-147 and TC-156 for the amendment. The four rows this sitting first-approves, and the four amendments it blesses, keep their rulings, because none of these changes touches their text.\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval\n"}}}
